From 72f0f2fb2ccf589a48973c8ad59bb3700770c521 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: matthane <matthan.evans@icloud.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 03:16:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] DVDInputStreamBluray: keep the title info at the end of a
 playlist

The end of the title frees the title info, as the playlist changes next
in navigation mode. Outside it the player still plays out its buffer and
can seek back, but total time, chapters and chapter seeks are then gone
for the rest of playback.

(cherry picked from xbmc/xbmc master 63362443735bd151c803662927503085fd3e46d3)

Hades: taken as it is. On Hades' tree a playlist played directly also goes
on its own timeline: a seek back after the end without the title info gave
its play item no place on it, and its packets kept their clip's clock.
Measured on a synthetic disc: after the end of a playlist of three play
items was read, the total time was 0 and there were no chapters while the
last packets played; with this change, the playlist's 12.011 s and its
3 chapters, and a seek back from there reads on, on the playlist's
timeline.
---
 .../cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.cpp
index 491ff91..3488a42 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.cpp
@@ -822,7 +822,8 @@ void CDVDInputStreamBluray::ProcessEvent() {
   case BD_EVENT_END_OF_TITLE:
     CLog::Log(LOGDEBUG, "CDVDInputStreamBluray - BD_EVENT_END_OF_TITLE {}", m_event.param);
     /* when a title ends, playlist WILL eventually change */
-    FreeTitleInfo();
+    if (m_navmode)
+      FreeTitleInfo();
     break;
 
   case BD_EVENT_TITLE:
